SECTION D — PARITY NOTES (web source is THE specification)
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
D1. Web-effect logic reproduced verbatim + unit-tested (A2):
      • firstRender guard — the initial route is NEVER announced (recorded, not scheduled): RouteAnnouncerModelTests
        .testInitialRouteIsSilentAndUnscheduled.
      • deferred read — `setTimeout(delayMs=100)` → RouteAnnounceScheduling seam; the read uses the SETTLED title
        (web: the lazy page's usePageTitle settles during the delay): .testDeferredReadSeesTheSettledTitle.
      • empty title → clear the region, silent, counter unchanged (web `setMessage('')`): .testEmptyTitleClears…
      • rotating 0–3 ZERO-WIDTH-SPACE suffix (`counter % 4`) so two routes with the SAME title both re-announce:
        RouteAnnouncerPadding + .testIdenticalConsecutiveTitlesBothReAnnounce.
      • cancel-pending on rapid navigation (web cleanup `clearTimeout`) — only the FINAL destination announces:
        .testRapidNavigationsCancelPendingAndOnlyFinalAnnounces.
      • custom delay (web `delayMs` prop): model `delay` parameter forwarded to the scheduler:
        .testModelForwardsConfiguredDelayToScheduler.
D2. Data sources: bound to the navigation feed (native useLocation peer = RouteAnnouncerNavigator) via the P1/S8
    RouteAnnouncerSource seam; no direct HTTP/router access from the view. The web source DELIBERATELY does not route
    through useAnnouncer (it documents why — route changes are declarative and need their own region); the native port
    mirrors that with its own RouteAnnouncementPresenter rather than the shared 0001 Announcer. The prompt's
    auto-listed "useAnnouncer" is superseded by the actual source, exactly as the web file states.
D3. Apple idiom: the web `<VisuallyHidden liveRegion priority="polite">` maps to
    AccessibilityNotification.Announcement at .default (polite) speech priority (ADR-009). The native parity surface
    additionally renders the region VISIBLY as a route-announcements inspector (the convention set by sibling 0001
    AnnouncerRegion) so every state is a real, non-blank UI while the real VoiceOver voicing happens through the
    presenter seam.
D4. States: the web source reads synchronous router state, so its intrinsic states are idle (suppressed initial route
    → empty hidden region) / announcing (title + padding voiced) / cleared (empty title). All are rendered; the P4
    leaf contract adds loading / error / stale / offline (freshness chip + one-shot stale auto-refresh) over the
    bound navigation feed, each a real surface (never a blank box). i18n (P1/S10): table "RouteAnnouncer", no English
    prose literal in code. Telemetry (P1/S11): view.opened emitted once with surface slug "RouteAnnouncer".
    Accessibility: VoiceOver labels on the region + history rows + the freshness button; Dynamic-Type semantic fonts;
    reduce-motion respected (no bespoke animation); localized region/history labels asserted by tests.

